    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        30
      ],
      "size": [
        620,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 4,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Snapshot: phone / analog-snapshot generation\n\nThe recipe behind a top-rated Krea 2 realism image: **Realistic Snapshot LoRA at 1.5**, euler / simple / **10 steps / CFG 1**, **768×1376**, a plain background and an analog-film line in the prompt.\n\n**Before the first run**\n- Pick your file in **Character LoRA** and put its trigger word at the start of the prompt.\n- Set her **real age** in the prompt (currently 25).\n\n**Varied camera angles:** sampling runs in two stages. Steps 0–3 (composition) use the character LoRA at only 0.3, so its selfie-angle habit can't lock the framing; steps 3–10 use it at 0.85 for likeness. Start the prompt with where the camera is.\n\n**What sells the realism:** simple settings (plain wall, bedroom, bathroom mirror) with nothing to render wrong, one light source you describe, and the \"analog shot… slight film grain and muted colors\" line. Busy scenes with signs and crowds undo it.\n\n**Then:** run the output through the realism pass if the skin needs more texture.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Snapshot: phone / analog-snapshot generation\n\nThe recipe behind a top-rated Krea 2 realism image: **Realistic Snapshot LoRA at 1.5**, euler / simple / **10 steps / CFG 1**, **768×1376**, a plain background and an analog-film line in the prompt.\n\n**Before the first run**\n- Pick your file in **Character LoRA** and put its trigger word at the start of the prompt.\n- Set her **real age** in the prompt (currently 25).\n\n**Varied camera angles:** sampling runs in two stages. Steps 0–3 (composition) use the character LoRA at only 0.3, so its selfie-angle habit can't lock the framing; steps 3–10 use it at 0.85 for likeness. Start the prompt with where the camera is.\n\n**What sells the realism:** simple settings (plain wall, bedroom, bathroom mirror) with nothing to render wrong, one light source you describe, and the \"analog shot… slight film grain and muted colors\" line. Busy scenes with signs and crowds undo it.\n\n**Then:** run the output through the realism pass if the skin needs more texture.\n"
      },
